course: dictionary
lesson: 14362
title: Words from the stage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from a special world, such as the theatre or music. Operatic is one of these. It comes from opera, a play where all or most of the words are sung, with an orchestra playing. «The orchestra tuned up before the opera began.» The clue is opera, so here operatic means to do with opera.
explain: Operatic can also describe behaviour. «She threw her arms up and gave an operatic sob when the bus drove away without her.» Nobody sings at a bus stop, but the sob is so big and dramatic that it seems to belong on a stage. Here operatic means very dramatic and over-the-top.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In the first example, "to do with opera" fits. In the bus example, "very dramatic" fits. If your meaning makes the sentence sensible, you are probably right.
fact: Operatic means to do with opera, or very dramatic and over-the-top.
fact: An opera is a play where all or most of the words are sung, with an orchestra.
fact: Operatic can describe a singer, a voice, an aria, or a big, dramatic display.
fact: «An operatic display of tears» means crying in a very dramatic way, more than the situation seems to need.
fact: Operatic is an adjective. Its comparison is more operatic.
exercise: «The tenor sang an operatic aria that filled the whole hall.» What does operatic mean here? | Very quiet and shy | *To do with opera, where the words are sung | Covered in paint | Cold and wet
exercise: Sam fell to the floor and gave an operatic groan because the match was cancelled. What does operatic suggest? | *Very dramatic and over-the-top | Hungry | Calm and quiet | Musical, with a nice tune
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to operatic when it means very dramatic? | Quiet | Calm | *Theatrical | Sleepy
test: «Her operatic sneeze made the whole class turn round.» What does operatic mean here? | Quiet and polite | *Very dramatic and over-the-top | Written in a book | Made of wood
test: Which of these is an operatic singer? | *A singer who performs the main parts in an opera | A cook who bakes bread | A builder who lays bricks
exam: Ruby says operatic means very old, like ancient. Is she right? | *No, it means to do with opera, or very dramatic | Yes, it means very old | Yes, it means very hungry
